# AC-03 declared failure 02 — access policy dropped from the incident list

Fictional data only.

## Diagnosis — broken state

listIncidents returns repository.list() without applying canViewIncident.

$ npm run typecheck   -> exit code 0
$ npm run lint        -> exit code 0
Type checking and style do not observe this regression. Only the control
test does, which is why each threat in the model is tied to a test.

$ npm run test:security
    × a reporter only lists the incidents they reported (4 ms)
    × a technician only lists the incidents assigned to them (1 ms)
    × an unrecognised role is denied by default (1 ms)
Test Suites: 1 failed, 1 total
Tests:       3 failed, 9 passed, 12 total

A reporter received campus-inc-002, reported by campus-reporter-202, and a
technician received campus-inc-001, which is not assigned to them. An
unrecognised role also received the whole backlog instead of nothing.
exit code: 1

## Corrected result

listIncidents applies canViewIncident again before returning the list.

$ npm run test:security
Test Suites: 1 passed, 1 total
Tests:       12 passed, 12 total
exit code: 0
